## 8. Latency Budget (example, consumer-facing SLA)

| Stage | Budget |
|---|---|
| Query understanding/embedding | ~20ms |
| Dense ANN search (fan-out + merge) | ~80ms |
| Sparse search (parallel) | ~30ms |
| Fusion | ~5ms |
| Reranking (cross-encoder on ~100 candidates) | ~100ms |
| Context assembly | ~10ms |
| LLM first-token latency | ~200ms |
| **Total to first token** | **~450ms** |
| Full generation (streamed) | 1-3s, hidden by streaming |

State clearly: dense search and reranking are almost always the two biggest levers if the SLA is missed — reranker candidate count (k) is a tunable quality/latency knob you'd point to first.

